---
description: Do not manually clean up GSAP tweens/ScrollTriggers inside useGSAP or useAnimation
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# GSAP Auto Cleanup

`useGSAP` (and the project's `useAnimation`, which wraps it with `gsap.matchMedia`) runs inside a `gsap.context()`. Every tween and ScrollTrigger created in the callback is automatically reverted on unmount or when a matchMedia condition stops matching.

Do **not** collect tweens to kill them, and do **not** return a cleanup function just to revert GSAP animations.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — redundant manual cleanup
useAnimation(({ isDesktop }) => {
	const tweens = items.map(el => gsap.fromTo(el, { opacity: 0 }, { opacity: 1, scrollTrigger: { trigger: el } }));

	return () => {
		tweens.forEach(t => {
			t.scrollTrigger?.kill();
			t.kill();
		});
	};
}, { scope: ref });

// ✅ GOOD — let the context revert everything
useAnimation(({ isDesktop }) => {
	items.forEach(el => {
        gsap.set(el, {
            autoAlpha: 0
        })
		gsap.fromTo(el, {
            autoAlpha: 1,
            scrollTrigger: {
                trigger: el,
                scroller,
                start: "top 100%",
                end: "bottom 0%",
                scrub: true,
                markers: false
            }
        });
	});
}, { scope: ref });
```

Only return a cleanup for non-GSAP resources (e.g. Lenis `Snap`, event listeners, `matchMedia` listeners) or for interaction-driven animations created outside the context.
